course: dictionary
lesson: 14681
title: What is a presidency?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A presidency is the job of being president, or the time that a person spends as president. Look inside the word: president. The ending tells you it is about that job or that time.
explain: «During his presidency, the school club built a new garden.» The words «during his» show a stretch of time, so presidency means the time he was president. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? The club built the garden while he was in charge.
explain: «Maya wants to run for the presidency of the school council.» To run for something means to try to win it. Winning the presidency means getting the top job, so you can see the word names a job people try to get.
fact: Presidency means the job of being president.
fact: A presidency can also mean the time during which a person is president.
fact: «Presidency» is a noun, and its plural is presidencies.
fact: In countries like the USA, France and Ireland, the presidency is the top job in the country.
fact: Clubs and companies can have a presidency too, and it is the top job there.
exercise: «During his presidency, the club won its first cup.» What does presidency mean here? | A school trip | A kind of cup | *The time he was president | A football pitch
exercise: «Maya wants to run for the presidency of the school council.» What does Maya want? | *To be president of the council | To buy a new bike | To clean the school hall | To leave the school council
exercise: What word is presidency built from? | precious | pretty | residency | *president
test: «She hopes to win the presidency next year.» What does win the presidency mean? | To join a new school | To lose all the club's money | To give a speech on Monday | *To become the president
test: Which word fits the gap? «The ___ of our club was a happy time.» | *presidency | ballet | puddle | pencil
exam: What is the plural of presidency? | *presidencies | presidences | presidencys | presidents
